WEBVTT

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.990
A special menu, just for exam season.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.450
The first dish is...

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.720
Exams start for real next month.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.810
I've got to give it my all!

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:11.520
No time for food! I have to focus!

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:16.400
What is that strange noise?

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.580
A monster!

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.830
I must have fallen asleep.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.720
Oh, I see. It's my tummy rumbling.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.520
Maybe I should take a break.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.980
<i>You're still up, Haruko?</i>

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.360
<i>Yeah, exams are getting close.</i>

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.730
Well, that's timely.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:58.700
<i>I'm glad to see you working so hard. Here's a midnight snack.</i>

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.660
<i>Ooh, what's the filling?</i>

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:06.950
<i>I wish my mom was here to make me snacks.</i>

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:11.170
<i>But Mom and Dad are both overseas, so...</i>

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:19.170
<i>My heart and my body each have their own reaction to the show.</i>

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:26.970
Mom and Dad are both working hard, though. I can't be selfish.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:32.230
Plus, I have Kirin and Shiina now.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:34.480
I'm not lonely at all.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:40.740
If anything, I'd just feel worse imposing on Mom when she's already so busy.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:45.780
Ms. Machiko! Package from overseas!

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.290
That might be from Mom!

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:51.330
Hi, Ryo!

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:55.840
Huh, your parents sent something?

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.800
Can I take a look?

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:01.510
I bet it's fancy candies from overseas!

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.090
The whole box smells Japanese.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:07.050
This is from Mom.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:13.480
"Looks like they just started selling ramen here, so I picked some up."

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:16.310
"Isn't that funny? I sent you some too."

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:18.570
Is she that impulsive?

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:24.110
Didn't she send Japanese rice last time?

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.820
You sure have interesting parents.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.080
It <i>is</i> kind of exciting to have this much, though.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.580
So, ramen for dinner tonight?

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.710
Of course not!

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:38.500
You eat ramen when you're using your noodle!

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.210
A midnight snack while studying for exams!

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.090
N-Noodle?

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:54.600
<i>Ryo looks serious today.</i>

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:59.690
Focus on studying, Ryo!

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:06.160
When you get a package from your parents, does it make you wish they were here?

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:08.370
A little.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:12.330
But I don't really feel any lonelier than I did before.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.370
Really?

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:14.120
Yep.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:20.130
They're really busy with work, too,
so I don't want to make them worry.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.710
I just want to get married right away and put their minds at ease!

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.930
No way! Just, no way!

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.220
I won't let that happen!

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.890
<i>Busy with work, huh?</i>

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:33.720
<i>Mom mentioned that.</i>

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:38.440
Ryo's parents?

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:43.110
If they quit, it'd be a loss for the whole city.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:44.940
What on Earth do they do?

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.320
The details are a secret.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:51.200
But they're worried about Ryo in their own way.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.830
They were going to get bodyguards for her.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.830
Isn't that just being overprotective?

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:02.340
<i>If Ryo had gotten bodyguards, I bet her personality would be completely different now.</i>

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.130
<i>She'd be haughtier.</i>

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.050
<i>Out of my way, pleb.</i>

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:07.510
<i>She'd have different habits.</i>

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:08.840
<i>Let's play soccer!</i>

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:12.510
<i>It's probably just as well she doesn't have them.</i>

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.470
<i>But what if they
change their mind?</i>

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:16.890
I don't want that!

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:20.690
From now on, Ryo, I'll be your bodyguard!

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:24.400
What's wrong, Kirin?

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.690
And where did you pull those sunglasses from?!

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.200
Why don't we take a break?

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.200
Great idea!

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.700
Time for a midnight snack!

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:40.370
I've been thinking about what the best way to eat this would be.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:41.330
And?

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:47.380
I think eating it raw is the best way to bring out its natural flavor.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.880
You overthought that so hard that you're back to square one.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:52.680
Don't worry. I'll make it.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.260
Really?

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:56.970
You've seemed kind of on edge today.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.940
And it's not like I've never made ramen before.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.190
Leave it to me!

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:04.440
Someone making me a midnight snack...

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.190
Oh, nothing. I'm just happy.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:08.440
Thanks in advance!

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.860
You can keep studying.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:13.320
Okay!

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.330
Ryo, you really love your parents, don't you?

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:25.340
All right, I'm gonna make this
just like a mother would!

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:30.340
Wait, my mom can't cook anything except veggie stir-fry!

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:35.720
At least she's good at that.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:39.430
<i>I wonder what Ryo's mother's cooking tastes like?</i>

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:43.440
<i>I have to be careful to make it just as she would!</i>

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.860
It's done!

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.900
Soy ramen with stir-fried veggies and an egg on top!

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:54.200
It looks delicious, if I do say so myself.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.120
Ryo, it's read—

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:01.870
Oh, did you fall asleep?

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:09.420
Wake up, Ryo. It's time for breakfast.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:10.880
Just kidding!

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.130
It's morning?

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:17.180
Mom!

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:19.720
Mom, I missed you!

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:20.520
Ryo?!

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:23.140
Look how much I've grown up!

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:25.600
I can cook now!

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.060
Mom...

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:30.440
You've gotten awfully small...

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.190
in more ways than one...

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.700
You're squeezing me, Ryo! Uncle! Uncle!

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.710
Sorry, I dozed off.

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.670
Don't misunderstand, though!

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:49.670
I was dreaming that the Earth was being invaded by aliens, and Mom was in trouble, and—

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:52.550
<i>Ryo really does miss her mom.</i>

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:56.470
Listen. I understand how you feel.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:02.730
But my perfectly prepared ramen is starting to get soggy,
so let's continue this conversation over a meal.

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.230
Sorry!

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:13.740
The veggies are simple and healthy, but still so appetizing.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:23.500
The noodles are a wonderful counterpoint to their crisp freshness <i>because</i> they've gotten a little soggy.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:29.380
And the soy-based broth and soft-boiled egg wrap around them so well.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:30.750
It's so... affectionate!

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:36.510
The slab bacon is so savory it makes my tongue tingle.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:41.760
And I could eat these fried noodles every day!

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:47.520
It's so tasty that I'm starting to forget what we were talking about!

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.270
<i>Amazing!</i>

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:55.240
Sorry about before, Kirin.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:56.530
I'm kind of embarrassed.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:57.740
Don't worry about it.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:01.450
You should say what you really feel instead of trying to hold it in.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:05.960
I'm kind of happy I was able to figure it out anyway, though.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:14.210
I'd be lying if I said I wasn't lonely at all,
but it's not that bad, honestly.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:14.960
Huh?

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:22.470
I'm really happy that you cooked the food she sent me.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.220
That's how I really feel.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:32.900
<i>It's not that bad, huh...</i>

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:38.530
<i>But I still hope she can spend time with her mom someday.</i>

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:43.410
A letter to m-me?

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:44.290
Top secret?

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:57.460
To Morino.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:00.510
Thanks for spending so much time with Ryo.

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:04.720
<i>I simply had to write to express my gratitude.</i>

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:08.020
<i>Ryo always writes about you in her letters.</i>

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:14.110
<i>I hope her impulsiveness hasn't caused you too much trouble</i>

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:16.860
<i>and that you'll continue to be good friends.</i>

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:21.860
<i>If necessary, I can hire bodyguards for you, so—</i>

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:23.870
Th-That won't be necessary!

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.370
I'm going to have to do it myself, aren't I?

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:34.790
<i>She really does worry about Ryo.</i>

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.130
<i>Why doesn't she just come to see her?</i>

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:38.960
<i>She must really be busy.</i>

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:43.760
<i>What kind of job wouldn't give her any time off?</i>

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.010
<i>So I asked.</i>

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:49.930
Huh? Mom's job?

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:51.310
Well...

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:56.570
She's important to the whole world....

00:11:56.570 --> 00:12:00.280
is about as much as I can tell you. Sorry.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.780
<i>I can't even ask?!</i>

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:04.990
<i>That was a total non-answer!</i>

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:09.040
A special menu, just for exam season.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:10.410
The second dish is...

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:19.050
<i>Exams start for real next week.</i>

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:26.350
May we go well on our exams next week!

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:30.350
I hope we can show the results of our hard work.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:32.980
I'd like to get rich.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.310
You're wishing for <i>that</i>? <i>Now</i>?

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:38.730
Why not make your wish about the exams? They're coming right up.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:42.110
Well, there's more to it than you think.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:48.280
Getting rich means getting into high school, getting into college, mastering a craft...

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:52.000
So if I were to put everything I hope for into just one wish...

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:54.040
I see. That's deep.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.250
Deep? It's just greedy!

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.800
I don't think anyone that materialistic will have any luck at all!

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.220
I wouldn't be surprised if you didn't even make it into high school.

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:06.590
Well, I don't need to worry about that anymore.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.180
<i>W-Wait...</i>

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:11.640
<i>Is she dropping out?</i>

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:15.020
There's something I need to tell you.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:20.150
I've already been accepted based on a recommendation.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:22.530
Same school as you two are hoping for.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:24.490
When did you take your test?

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:25.900
Don't scare us like that!

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:28.450
You made us worry!
Why didn't you tell us?

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.620
Sorry, one at a time, please.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:34.370
When were you accepted?!

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:36.250
At the beginning of the month.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.330
That's not fair, you cheater!

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:40.420
How is it not fair?

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:44.170
I worked hard all by myself studying for that test.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:47.180
Y-You should have told us!

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:48.550
I already apologized.

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:51.510
Are you even listening?! Ryo, you tell—

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:53.270
Congratulations!

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:57.730
I'm so happy for you!
It must have been a lot of work.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.150
You did really, really well!

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:02.320
This is such a relief!

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:03.360
It definitely casts who truly has a good heart into relief.

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:07.400
I'm so happy for you! Congrats!

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.780
Let me in too!

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.040
Kirin?

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:16.500
I'm happy Shiina already made it in too,

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:19.920
but it wasn't very nice to keep it a secret!

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.090
Kirin.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:28.800
Why don't you say what you really feel?

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:32.050
Cong...

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:34.060
What was that? I didn't hear you.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.310
Congratulations! Congratulations!

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:41.440
Congratu-contula-contulagra-nios!

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.940
Sorry, sorry. I get it.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:51.620
Look at these cute charms!

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.580
They really are cute! Let's buy some!

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:56.700
Let's see. Charms to make you pass,

00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:00.420
five-sided pencils, ones for safe travel...

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:01.960
Ones for exorcism too.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:06.460
And here are ones for domestic tranquility, ones for finding love, and erasers to help you pass!

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:14.470
I guess the more you have,
the more good they do, right?

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:16.970
You're pretty greedy too, Morino.

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:21.230
I thought I could use a little divine favor.

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.730
Here, Shiina.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:25.230
To celebrate your success.

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:26.730
It'll give you luck in your studies.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:28.610
Thank you.

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:31.820
Why is it all about Shiina?

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:35.240
She should buy some for us too!

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.370
Nope.

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:37.370
You didn't even consider it!

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.830
I mean, if you say "too," that just means I should buy one for Machiko.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:43.130
That's true...

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:45.670
But you've already gotten in!

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:48.300
Now you should be cheering <i>us</i> on!

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:50.420
I don't think that's healthy.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:52.930
That's a cold, cold stare.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:56.430
You're so cold today, Shiina.

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:58.430
It's like you're completely rejecting me!

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:00.310
It's not like that.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:01.810
It's just...

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:05.440
Exams are a battle you have to fight on your own, right?

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:10.240
Before you rely on the gods, or on other people,

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:11.990
you have to rely on yourself.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:13.860
That's a bit <i>too</i> true.

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:17.990
Is that why you didn't mention the priority testing?

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:22.750
<i>Normally I'd just be mad, but there's no way I can argue with her now.</i>

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:27.250
Stop doing that thing with your hands.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:29.670
Why?!

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:32.170
If you just did a little bit to cheer me on,
I could try so much harder!

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:34.380
You don't need it, though.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:39.060
So you're saying you did it all by yourself?

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.850
I certainly wouldn't say I didn't.

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:46.230
You idiot! You don't even understand how much it can help!

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:46.980
You're too damn stoic!

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:52.150
Could you two please stop rubbing me all over?

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:55.360
But maybe your luck will rub off on us!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:04.290
Sometimes people just don't agree on things.

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:05.420
But—

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.130
Are you hungry?

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.380
I brought lunch. Let's eat.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:13.720
Oh, so now you're trying to bribe me with food?

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:16.010
I refuse! This is a matter of pride!

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:19.390
Are you sure? It's Tsuyuko's best.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:22.020
Guess I'll just have to split it with Machiko.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:25.270
Your pride doesn't go far, huh?

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:28.400
No, but Tsuyuko's cooking goes a long way.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.440
She's like, three-star-chef level.

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:39.030
Juicy cutlet sandwiches!

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:41.660
Look at the meat just crammed into the bread!

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:44.910
What?

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:50.380
You say you did it all on your own,
but you're pretty superstitious yourself,

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:52.420
going for cutlets so you can make it above the cut.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:55.420
This was just Tsuyuko's idea.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:58.840
They're packed!

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:01.850
She made enough for us too?

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:12.070
The fluffy, buttered bread, the crisp cabbage, and the moist cutlet...

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:15.860
They're like a symphonic golden ratio of textures!

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.240
Delicious enough to take you out of this world,

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:25.370
but then the bite of the pepper brings you back.

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:32.750
Springy bread, springy meat...

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.880
It's like a one-two springy punch giving me strength!

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.930
They have such an incredible aura of life!

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:41.390
Just what are they?!

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:45.890
This is definitely Tsuyuko's cooking. I could just melt.

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:49.020
It's what I've been snacking on lately.

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:50.480
You're so lucky.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:55.610
If I had these to snack on,
they'd keep me going, even on my own.

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:59.360
See, Shiina? She's definitely cheering you on.

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:04.240
Really? She said she was just in the mood to make cutlets.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:06.240
<i>I can't tell her.</i>

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:13.710
<i>I can't possibly tell her that I spent an hour after cooking trying to give them that "try-hard!" aura.</i>

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:19.510
I understand what you mean, though.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:22.760
<i>She made sandwiches like
these on the day of my exam.</i>

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.020
Oh, a cutlet sandwich again.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:34.560
<i>I felt like I was going into the exams alone,</i>

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:40.280
<i>but I forgot how, when I saw the sandwich,
it was like seeing Tsuyuko's face in front of me.</i>

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:49.540
<i>It pulled me out of the funk I was in and made me feel like trying again.</i>

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:56.210
<i>I guess it really wasn't all me.</i>

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:02.300
Shall we go up one more time to be sure?

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:03.300
Agreed!

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:04.390
So, uh.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:13.400
I'm sorry. I was still so caught up in my exams that I said things that I shouldn't have.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:15.900
Shiina...

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:20.650
If there's anything you want to know about the exam, just ask.

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:27.160
Well... Where are the bathrooms?

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:30.040
That's it? <i>That's</i> all you want to know?

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:31.870
Well, it wouldn't be good if I couldn't find them.

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:34.670
She's right. It <i>is</i> pretty important.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:40.170
<i>And the day of exams...</i>

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.550
Do you have everything, Kirin?

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:43.930
I-I think so.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.310
My stomach hurts.

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:50.890
Just calm down.

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:54.140
Morning.

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:58.400
What are you doing here this early, Shiina?

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:02.030
I made lunch for you.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.280
<i>You</i> made lunch?

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:05.950
Yeah, Tsuyuko showed me—

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:11.160
Why are you trembling like that?

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:14.080
W-We really appreciate it...

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:18.170
But it's so unlike you that it feels like we just used up all our luck.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:20.050
Don't be so negative.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:24.220
You'll be fine. Tsuyuko's cutlet sandwiches will give you luck,

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:26.300
just like they gave me luck.

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:29.050
Thanks!

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:32.560
Here we go!

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:42.530
Cutlet sandwiches?

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:46.280
Yeah. I'd like to give them some on exam day.

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:47.660
Is there a trick to it?

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:50.240
Well, there's...

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:53.120
the "try-hard!" aura...

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:56.160
Er, nothing.

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:07.800
Try hard, try hard, try hard...

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:11.050
Try hard, try hard, try hard, try hard, try hard, try hard, try hard...

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:45.650
So you shave down the corners a little?

00:23:45.650 --> 00:23:48.940
If you trim the edges, it keeps it from falling apart while boiling.

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:51.910
Wow, cooking is complicated.

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:53.740
It's not a big deal.

00:23:53.740 --> 00:23:59.370
You just have to imagine the happy face of someone you care for very, very much.

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:01.080
Someone you care for...

00:24:04.420 --> 00:24:06.960
Next time on Gourmet Girl Graffiti:

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:09.010
Marinated and Hearty!
